    "result": "Perfect! The feature is fully implemented and working. Let me summarize what I've done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `renderSummary` feature for the frai-gate package:\n\n### 1. **Added `renderSummary()` function** to `src/gate/report.ts`\n   - Returns a one-line summary: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>`\n   - Total is always 7 (the number of GATE_CHECKS)\n   - Answered count excludes checks with block-severity findings\n   - When there are block findings, appends the check IDs in GATE_CHECKS order\n   - Special case: returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when the gate section is missing\n\n### 2. **Added `--summary` flag** to `frai-gate check` command\n   - Prints only the summary line instead of the full text report\n   - Exit codes remain the same (1 for BLOCK, 0 for PASS/WARN)\n   - `--json` flag takes priority if both are specified\n   - Updated usage message and help text\n\n### 3. **Added comprehensive tests** in `src/gate/report.test.ts`\n   - 8 new test cases covering all scenarios:\n     - PASS with all checks answered\n     - WARN with warnings only\n     - BLOCK with specific check IDs\n     - Structure finding special case\n     - Check ID ordering and deduplication\n     - Mixed blocks and warnings\n\n### 4. **Exported the new function** from `src/index.ts` for public API access\n\n### Test Results\n- \u2705 All 19 tests pass (8 new + 11 existing)\n- \u2705 Package builds successfully with no TypeScript errors\n- \u2705 CLI help text correctly documents the new flag\n\nThe implementation is production-ready and fully tested.",
